user: Right now we have borders along both left and right edges, but perhaps it would be enough with just the top. That goes for both the transcript and prompt areas, which should allow one more line of content for each area. We'd like to have an always available scrollbar along the right edge, that is adaptive to the position and size of the current window into the full transcript output.
I'd like to have the standard black background color for all output, except for thinking content and highlighted code content. For thinking content I'd like to have a left edge, plus the different background color. While for highlighted code areas we have an indentation plus a background color. This should make those areas stand out suitably. Do you think it is good to have an edge, and indentation, in these cases?
I want a good looking output, that is easy to read and pleasant to look at. Make sure we have a good default theme, plus at least a light alternative, for those what want that. Also document the theming support. Does this make sense and provide a pleasing, readable layout with enough contrast and cues to quickly differentiate between different content. Please contemplate, advise and implement. Commit once done. Thanks

