Note: a hidden run was stored as a complete contiguous run — the first line of the run had the FIRST edge, and the rest had CONT. After re-wrapping, each re-wrapped block gets the edge pattern based on its own index — the first wrap gets FIRST, and the rest get CONT. This is consistent with how push_reasoning_lines builds it.

